# The build context is what the Dockerfile copies and nothing else:
# pyproject.toml and README.md (the package metadata), api/, config/,
# web/ (the frontend sources and its lock file) and the release notes the
# docs site renders (docs/_data/releases.yml). Everything else stays out:
# the git history, the virtualenv, node_modules, local data (the MITM CA,
# IP database files), tests, docs, editor and tool caches, and .env with
# its secrets. A COPY of anything new needs a line here.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!api
!config
!web
!docs/_data/releases.yml

# Inside the copied directories: dependencies the build installs itself,
# build output, bytecode and editor droppings.
web/node_modules
web/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
